resize-hfs contains original code from the author's legacy iOS storage
research, carried forward into a standalone project on 28 October 2026.

The source relies on Apple's public HFS Plus Volume Format documentation
and public UEFI GPT field/checksum definitions. macOS experiments call the
host's filesystem implementation through its system interfaces.

Apple's HFS source is an APSL-2.0 research reference. danzatt/hfs_resize
and openiBoot are GPL research references. Their implementations and Apple
firmware are not included in this repository. Source notes record the
boundaries of the imported Swift fixtures and their assumptions.
